SUMMARY:Rooms of Becoming Reception
DESCRIPTION:The Barn Gallery’s upcoming exhibition\, Rooms of Becoming: Studio Studies of Northern California Artists\, will hold a reception on Saturday\, November 21\, from 2-5pm. Meet the artists and enjoy light refreshments during this event\, which is free and open to the public. The Gibson House will also be open until 4 p.m. \nRooms of Becoming brings together the work of two photographers tasked with documenting the creative environments of five Northern California artists. \nCurated by Tomás Montoya and displaying photography by Andres Alvarez and Roberta Alvarado\, this exhibition features painter and sculptor Craig Martinez\, writer and journalist Liv Styler\, tattoo artist Butch Felix\, and culinary artists Nick Duren and Whitney Johnson. \nPhotographic documentation and artwork from each artist will offer viewers intimate access to the sites where imagination takes form. \nRooms of Becoming is on view at The Barn Gallery November 14\, 2026 through January 16\, 2027. Regular open hours of The Barn Gallery are Tuesdays\, Wednesdays\, and Thursdays from 12 – 5 p.m. and Saturdays from 12 – 3 p.m. \nRegular open hours of The Gibson House are Tuesdays and Thursdays from 12 – 4 p.m. and every third Saturday from 8 a.m. – 4 p.m. \nThe Barn Gallery and the Gibson House are located at 512 Gibson Road in Woodland. For more information\, visit www.yoloarts.org\, or contact ya@yoloarts.org or 530-309-6464.
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/rooms-of-becoming-reception/
LOCATION:The Barn Gallery\, 512 Gibson Road\, Woodland\, CA\, United States
