SUMMARY:UC Davis Concert Band
DESCRIPTION:The UC Davis Concert Band kicks off their 2026–27 season at the Robert and Margrit Mondavi Center for the Performing Arts. Concert Band takes the stage on Saturday\, Nov. 21 at 5 p.m. The UC Davis Concert Band celebrates its 75th anniversary as does guest ensemble California Youth Symphony whose Wind Symphony performs as part of the event. Pete Nowlen serves as director of both Concert Band and the Wind Symphony. The performance also features an appearance from the McClatchy High School Concert Band\, directed by Jorge Muñoz. The celebratory concert’s program includes Leonard Bernstein: Suite from “Candide\,” Toshio Masimo’s “Formosa\,” Li Chan’s “Folksong of Midu” and Tim Mahr’s “Diamond Celebration.” \nTickets for each concert are $13 for UC Davis students; $17 for children (under 18)\, $27 for faculty/staff and $30 adults.
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/uc-davis-concert-band/
LOCATION:Mondavi Center (Mondavi) UC Davis Campus
CATEGORIES:Music
